From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 00:11:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cmake: drop the ARM-only -mno-neon flag on non-ARM, non-x86
 targets

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [riscv64 is neither ARM nor x86; -mno-neon is a GCC ARM-backend-only flag and fails to configure on riscv64]

The NGT_AVX_DISABLED/NGT_SIMD_DISABLED Release branch picks the portable
non-SIMD distance-computation path (PrimitiveComparatorNoArch.h is
selected whenever neither __x86_64__ nor NGT_NEON is defined, see
lib/NGT/PrimitiveComparator.h) on every architecture, but its final
else() -- meant for 32-bit ARM, where disabling NEON needs an explicit
flag -- unconditionally appends -mno-neon regardless of the actual
target. GCC rejects that flag outright on riscv64
("unrecognized command-line option '-mno-neon'"), aborting the
configure step before any NGT/riscv64-specific code is even reached.
Drop the flag for this branch; the aarch64/arm64 branch above already
shows the same compile-options list works with no extra flag once SIMD
is disabled.

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 CMakeLists.txt | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index 8be7119..d3cfc66 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -87,8 +87,8 @@ if(${UNIX})
                         message(STATUS "ARM64 detected: NEON is mandatory, disable SIMD logically")
                         add_compile_options(-O3 -ffast-math -DNDEBUG)
 		    else()
-                        message(STATUS "NEON will not be used to compute distances.")
-                        add_compile_options(-O3 -ffast-math -mno-neon -DNDEBUG)
+                        message(STATUS "Not an ARM/x86 target: no arch-specific SIMD flag needed.")
+                        add_compile_options(-O3 -ffast-math -DNDEBUG)
                     endif()
                 endif()
             else()
-- 
